    "text": "Here's the implementation of the function `even_odd_count()`:\n\n```python\ndef even_and_odd_count(num):\n    \"\"\"Given an integer, return a tuple that contains the number\n    even and odd digits respectively.\n\n    Example:\n        even_odd_count(-12) ==> (1, 1)\n        even_odd_count(123) ==> (1, 2)\n    \"\"\"\n    for digit in str(num):\n        if int(digit) == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n    return (even_count, odd_count)\n\n```\n\nThis function works by converting the integer to a string, then iterating over each digit, and counting the number of even and odd digits.",
